# Extra disks of the KubeVirt VM (talos-gitops k8s/virtualmachines/homeserver-vm): blank virtio disks found by their serial. Docs: docs/homeserver/README.md.
# x-systemd.makefs formats a blank disk once, x-systemd.growfs follows an expanded volume, x-systemd.mkdir creates the mount point and nofail lets a VM without
# the disks (a bare-metal or libvirt run) boot all the same.
# The home disk replaces /var/home (/home): the account and its dotfiles are made on it at the first boot. Recreating the VM starts from a blank one.
/dev/disk/by-id/virtio-home       /var/home       xfs  defaults,nofail,x-systemd.makefs,x-systemd.growfs,x-systemd.device-timeout=10s  0 0
# Scratch that may be lost at any time. /workspace is a link to it (the root is read-only on a bootc system).
/dev/disk/by-id/virtio-workspace  /var/workspace  xfs  defaults,nofail,x-systemd.makefs,x-systemd.growfs,x-systemd.mkdir,x-systemd.device-timeout=10s  0 0
